# ── Local data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything under the repo-root data/ is local cache or bootstrap output —
# never tracked.
#
# ⚠ The leading slash matters and was missing. A bare `data/` is matched at
# EVERY depth, so it also ignored `packages/py/reimagina/data/` — the Python
# package. The files already there stayed tracked (gitignore does not untrack),
# which hid the problem completely: `data/feature.py`, `data/aoi.py` and the
# rest kept working, while two NEW modules in the same package,
# `data/roads.py` and `data/attribution.py`, were silently skipped by
# `git add -A` and shipped to nobody. A fresh clone raised
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'reimagina.data.roads'` the first time
# anyone ran `network bootstrap`.
# Bootstrap procedure to re-fetch is documented in docs/BOOTSTRAP.md.
/data/

# ── Environment / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Timestamped copies made before editing .env. They carry the same DSNs as the
# real file and are not covered by the patterns above, so they would otherwise
# be offered up as untracked files at the next `git add`.
.env.backup-*
!.env.example

